{{- /*
login.gohtml is the panel's sign-in form.

The body is sent urlencoded and parsed in the panel's OWN handler; it never
reaches the JSON endpoint. The concrete consequence is that the admin endpoints'
strict body decoder — the one that rejects unknown fields — never runs here:
form field names are the panel's business, not the API contract's.

The error message is printed conditionally and is an ordinary field, so escaping
applies to it as well. Field-level validation errors do not exist in the
framework, so a single box is shown.

The hidden "next" field is the page the operator was interrupted on. It is
attacker-influenceable by construction, so it is checked AGAIN on the way out
(safeReturnTarget) rather than trusted because this template wrote it; what the
template contributes is the escaping every field here gets.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>Sign in</h1>
{{ if .Error }}<p role="alert">{{ .Error }}</p>{{ end }}
<form method="post" action="{{ .LoginPath }}">
  {{ if .Next }}<input type="hidden" name="next" value="{{ .Next }}">{{ end }}
  <label>Email
    <input type="email" name="email" value="{{ .Email }}" required autocomplete="username">
  </label>
  <label>Password
    <input type="password" name="password" required autocomplete="current-password">
  </label>
  <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
</form>
{{ end }}
